     "text": "Three thousand lines of manual assembly code were required just to draw a blue rectangle on a screen in nineteen ninety. Engineers believed mastering software meant memorizing thousands of rigid syntax rules and pointer operations. Manual memory management ruled early engineering. Exact low level execution demanded endless focus. Then generative models arrived. Now modern artificial intelligence produces functional app codebases directly from plain language prompts. Vibe coding completely flips this paradigm. Developers replace manual typing with direct intent. This turns developers into creative editors. Engineers using generative AI coding tools complete tasks up to fifty five percent faster. Speed changes everything. Modern developer workflows shift from manual syntax authoring. System architecture validation takes center stage. Syntax is dead."
